    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">NHRSAP elaborated and adopted;
National Mechanism for PwDs created and operational;
Amendments to PDP regulations ensuring GDPR compliance are adopted;
At least one guideline for PDO on monitoring human rights situation (in selected fields) is elaborated;
Institutional Development Plan of SIS elaborated;
At least 50 people benefiting from mental health services through primary care piloted in Tbilisi;</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The draft of National Human Rights Strategy for 2021-2030 is elaborated. Due to the political turbulences and change in the management of the Government the elaboration and adoption of the Strategy is delayed. It is promised by the Government that the Strategy will be adopted in the first half of 2022.
Coordination Commission responsible on the implementation of CRPD in Georgia was established in November 2021. First Session of the Commission was conducted on 3 December 2021.
Draft law on PDP aligned with the requirements of GDPR is submitted to the Parliament and its adoption is delayed.
The draft Institutional Development Strategy of the SIS is elaborated to be adopted in the beginning of 2022.
Cooperation with PDO has started. After discussions with Deputy Public Defenders it was decided to elaborate guideline on monitoring of exercise of right to health. The elaboration process will start in 2022.
Under the RPA with NGO &#x201c;Global Initiative in Psychiatry &#x2013; Tbilisi&#x201d;, supported elaboration of training materials and programme and delivered the ToT for PHC personal from Batumi, Gori and Tbilisi to develop their skills and integrate MH care in their work. GIP has started providing regular supervisions for PHC staff to deliver MH Services.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
